there are 41 navigations (1 search + 40 listings), so the log was cleared before it and nothing else has run yet. Here’s how to read each column:

burst 14, ok: about one page per second gives 14 in a 10 s window, far under 100. The rule correctly leaves it alone, and this is your false-positive check passing.
gap_ms 946 and cv 0.43: the delay in the script is uniform(0.2, 1.5), and a uniform spread like that gives a CV of about 0.44, so the 0.43 is just the script’s random generator showing through. Real people have much heavier tails: many quick clicks, then a long pause to read. I’d expect your real Firefox to show a noticeably higher number, so don’t choose a threshold for cv until you’ve seen it.
seq% 0: the IDs are random, so no sequential steps. That’s the human-like part of this script.
noref% 100: this is where human_sim is unlike a person. It’s httpx, which never sends a referer. A person clicking through pages would show far less than 100.
